      "side": 1,
      "message": "If your concern is that the importing of cc/linkerconfig here, I could move them to linkerconfig package.\nBut in any way, we probably need some kind of \"linker_config -\u003e filesystem\" or \"filesystem -\u003e linker_config\" dependency. It\u0027s because not every PackagingBase needs linker.config.pb(cvd hosting tools doesn\u0027t).\n\nI\u0027m thinking of that\n- filesystem doesn\u0027t do anything special about linker.config.pb (or linker_config module)\n- linker_config module knows about \"filesystem\" and when has a callback to be called in PackagingBase.CopyDepsToZip. (Of course this should be an interface like `ContentDescriber`(?)), in which it generates linker.config.pb with stub libraries.\n- PackagingBase calls ContentDescriber.Describe(deps) with the collected \"deps\". This way, we can easily add a new content describing module to any of PackagingBase. (e.g. \"installed-files.txt\" in the package)",
